From 93f16155d7742cb369537ba6a359aae0c6ec3ad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:16:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v2.0.1: fix Samba 4 account enrollment - smbpasswd
 needs -c /etc/smb.conf

Metal (owner RT-BE96U, v2.0.1): smbd started fine but NO login worked -> every
session dropped to guest -> "Encryption is not supported for guest access".
Root cause: /etc/samba/smbpasswd came up EMPTY on boot even though the account
list has users. start_samba() enrolls accounts with `smbpasswd -s -a <user>`,
but WITHOUT -c the tool uses Samba 4's compiled default config path
(/etc/samba/smb.conf, per `smbd -b`), not this build's /etc/smb.conf -- so it
wrote the passdb to the wrong place and smbd's own passdb (smb passwd file =
/etc/samba/smbpasswd, read via `smbd -s /etc/smb.conf`) stayed empty. Result:
account-mode shares (valid users = <acct>) rejected every login.

Fix: pass `-c /etc/smb.conf` on all three SAMBA4 smbpasswd enrollment calls
(nobody + PMS-account loop + acc_list loop) so entries land in the passdb smbd
actually reads. Verified on metal: `smbpasswd -c /etc/smb.conf -a admin`
populated /etc/samba/smbpasswd and the Windows `net use /user:admin` mounted the
share. (SAMBA36X paths use the old `smbpasswd "user" "pass"` form and are
untouched.)

Completes the Samba 4 fix set: lib path (ld.so.conf) + runtime dirs +
map-to-guest + this enrollment fix = SMB works out of the box.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/usb.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/usb.c b/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
index 355b359bae0..2a88dd95974 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
@@ -3520,7 +3520,7 @@ start_samba(void)
 	//system("echo -e \"\n\n\" |/usr/sbin/smbpasswd -s -a nobody");
 	system("/usr/sbin/smbpasswd nobody \"\"");
 #elif defined(RTCONFIG_SAMBA4)
-	system("echo -e \"\n\n\" |/usr/sbin/smbpasswd -s -a nobody");
+	system("echo -e \"\n\n\" |/usr/sbin/smbpasswd -c /etc/smb.conf -s -a nobody");
 #else
 	system("smbpasswd nobody \"\"");
 #endif
@@ -3562,7 +3562,7 @@ start_samba(void)
 					close(_pfd[1]);
 					dup2(_pfd[0], STDIN_FILENO);
 					close(_pfd[0]);
-					execl("/usr/sbin/smbpasswd", "smbpasswd", "-s", "-a", char_user, (char *)NULL);
+					execl("/usr/sbin/smbpasswd", "smbpasswd", "-c", "/etc/smb.conf", "-s", "-a", char_user, (char *)NULL);	/* reaper v2.0.1: Samba 4 needs the config path */
 					_exit(127);
 				} else if (_pid > 0) {
 					close(_pfd[0]);
@@ -3654,7 +3654,7 @@ start_samba(void)
 						close(_pfd[1]);
 						dup2(_pfd[0], STDIN_FILENO);
 						close(_pfd[0]);
-						execl("/usr/sbin/smbpasswd", "smbpasswd", "-s", "-a", char_user, (char *)NULL);
+						execl("/usr/sbin/smbpasswd", "smbpasswd", "-c", "/etc/smb.conf", "-s", "-a", char_user, (char *)NULL);	/* reaper v2.0.1: Samba 4 needs the config path */
 						_exit(127);
 					} else if (_pid > 0) {
 						close(_pfd[0]);
-- 
